1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,180
A number of years ago my parents were

2
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:05,599
zoche to purchase an apartment in Eretz Yisrael

3
00:00:07,099 --> 00:00:09,880
and that opened up a whole new series

4
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:13,000
of shailos about how to relate to time

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,439
that they spend in Eretz Yisrael. It makes

6
00:00:15,439 --> 00:00:16,699
my life a lot better when I go

7
00:00:16,699 --> 00:00:17,980
to Eretz Yisrael that I have a home

8
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:20,420
to stay at that's sort of, not exactly

9
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:21,899
my own, but sort of my own, but

10
00:00:21,899 --> 00:00:23,179
it raises a whole bunch of shailos. So

11
00:00:23,179 --> 00:00:25,019
the first shaila, the first issue that was

12
00:00:25,019 --> 00:00:26,839
omed al haperek for them was that now

13
00:00:26,839 --> 00:00:28,019
that they own a place in Eretz Yisrael,

14
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:30,140
they still own their home that I grew

15
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:32,119
up in and live there most of the

16
00:00:32,119 --> 00:00:33,759
year, but now that they have an apartment

17
00:00:33,759 --> 00:00:35,600
in Eretz Yisrael, what do they do about

18
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:37,560
two days of Yom Tov? So this has

19
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:41,519
become an increasingly complicated issue about how Bnei

20
00:00:41,519 --> 00:00:43,340
Chutz La'aretz should deal with two days of

21
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:45,619
Yom Tov and I'm not discussing that now.

22
00:00:45,759 --> 00:00:47,859
We've had a halacha shiur on that and

23
00:00:47,859 --> 00:00:49,880
how Bnei Chutz La'aretz should deal with two

24
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:51,539
days of Yom Tov. What we're discussing today

25
00:00:51,539 --> 00:00:54,140
is are they Bnei Chutz La'aretz or not?

26
00:00:54,140 --> 00:00:56,009
Meaning, when you own an apartment in Eretz

27
00:00:56,009 --> 00:00:58,240
Yisrael does that change anything? Does that make

28
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:02,039
you a Ben Eretz Yisrael? So in order

29
00:01:02,039 --> 00:01:03,579
to, so what I'm going to share with

30
00:01:03,579 --> 00:01:07,033
you today is an approach that Rav Asher

31
00:01:07,033 --> 00:01:10,079
Weiss printed in the latest volume of Yeshurun,

32
00:01:10,219 --> 00:01:11,920
a teshuvah he wrote that was printed in

33
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:13,519
the latest volume of Yeshurun. I imagine it

34
00:01:13,519 --> 00:01:15,819
will be forthcoming in one of his Minchas

35
00:01:15,819 --> 00:01:19,640
Asher but for now it's in the Yeshurun

36
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:22,640
journal and I thought that his approach resonated

37
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,739
very much with me to the point that

38
00:01:24,739 --> 00:01:26,459
my parents never asked me the shaila but

39
00:01:26,459 --> 00:01:28,680
someone else who's in a similar situation had

40
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:30,459
asked me the shaila and my netiya right

41
00:01:30,459 --> 00:01:33,340
away was to say a very similar svara

42
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:35,359
to what Rav Asher Weiss suggests. I just

43
00:01:35,359 --> 00:01:36,879
didn't have the guts to say it, but

44
00:01:36,879 --> 00:01:38,079
now that I know that Rav Asher Weiss

45
00:01:38,079 --> 00:01:40,760
says it, I have the guts to say

46
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:43,340
you could rely on Rav Asher Weiss. So

47
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:45,959
here's, here's his approach. He starts off by

48
00:01:45,959 --> 00:01:47,969
telling us there's a teshuvah in the Avkas

49
00:01:47,969 --> 00:01:49,840
Rochel. The Avkas Rochel of course was written

50
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:52,280
by the Beis Yosef. In Siman Chaf-vav he

51
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:54,710
writes that Bnei Chutz La'aretz who are oleh

52
00:01:54,710 --> 00:01:57,900
leregel observe two days of Yom Tov in

53
00:01:57,900 --> 00:02:00,819
Eretz Yisrael and they davin b'farhesya and he

54
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:04,618
says v'davar zeh na'aseh me'az u'mikedem lifnei gedolei

55
00:02:04,618 --> 00:02:07,280
olam v'ein potzeh peh u'metzaftzef. And that's always

56
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,780
been the minhag, it's been done for a

57
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:10,800
long, long time. No one ever argues about

58
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,379
it, no one ever has a taina. If

59
00:02:12,379 --> 00:02:13,979
a ben Chutz La'aretz spends Yom Tov in

60
00:02:13,979 --> 00:02:16,159
Eretz Yisrael and keeps two days, he's fully

61
00:02:16,159 --> 00:02:18,020
within his rights and he's doing the right

62
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:19,400
thing and he can davin a Yom Tov

63
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:22,120
davening on the second day. Chida writes this

64
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:23,710
way in Birkei Yosef Siman Taf-tzadi-vav, the Pa'as

65
00:02:23,710 --> 00:02:25,517
Ha-shulchan in Hilchos Eretz Yisrael Perek Beis Sif

66
00:02:25,517 --> 00:02:29,060
Tes-vav. That is the, that is the accepted

67
00:02:29,060 --> 00:02:32,520
practice. However, there are three different approaches that

68
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:34,699
all suggest that a ben Chutz La'aretz and

69
00:02:34,699 --> 00:02:36,460
again, that's not really our topic, but we

70
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:38,219
have to have some familiarity with it in

71
00:02:38,219 --> 00:02:39,780
order to get to our topic, there are

72
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:42,020
three different approaches to suggest that a ben

73
00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:45,219
Chutz La'aretz in Eretz Yisrael does not keep

74
00:02:45,219 --> 00:02:47,219
two days of Yom Tov. And even though

75
00:02:47,219 --> 00:02:50,159
we don't accept these three different approaches, it's

76
00:02:50,159 --> 00:02:52,159
important to be familiar with them. One of

77
00:02:52,159 --> 00:02:54,800
them is the Chacham Tzvi. The Chacham Tzvi

78
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:58,099
in Chelek Aleph Siman Kuf-samech-zayin writes that since

79
00:02:58,099 --> 00:03:00,759
a ben Eretz Yisrael is not allowed to

80
00:03:00,759 --> 00:03:03,340
be mosif an extra day of Yom Tov

81
00:03:03,419 --> 00:03:05,180
it would be a violation of the issur

82
00:03:05,180 --> 00:03:08,319
of bal tosef, so the whole notion that

83
00:03:08,319 --> 00:03:10,659
you keep the chumrei hamakom when you travel

84
00:03:10,659 --> 00:03:12,719
from one place to another, that you observe

85
00:03:12,719 --> 00:03:14,180
the chumros of the place that you came

86
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:15,439
from and the chumros of the place that

87
00:03:15,439 --> 00:03:17,719
you come to, that's when observing your chumra

88
00:03:17,719 --> 00:03:19,659
is only a chumra. But if you're going

89
00:03:19,659 --> 00:03:21,509
to say that oh, I've come from Chutz

90
00:03:21,509 --> 00:03:22,819
La'aretz and now I'm in Eretz Yisrael so

91
00:03:22,819 --> 00:03:25,039
I'm going to still observe the chumra of

92
00:03:25,039 --> 00:03:27,120
Chutz La'aretz of keeping two days, well in

93
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:29,060
Eretz Yisrael that's not a chumra, that's a

94
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:31,620
kula because it's a violation of bal tosef

95
00:03:31,620 --> 00:03:33,960
for Bnei Eretz Yisrael to do that. And

96
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:36,319
therefore says the Chacham Tzvi Bnei Chutz La'aretz

97
00:03:36,319 --> 00:03:38,680
who visit Eretz Yisrael do not keep two

98
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:40,900
days of Yom Tov because we cannot apply

99
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:42,939
the rule of keeping the chumros of the

100
00:03:42,939 --> 00:03:46,599
place from where you came. A similar but

101
00:03:46,599 --> 00:03:48,979
different svara is offered by the son of

102
00:03:48,979 --> 00:03:52,080
the Chacham Tzvi Rav Yaakov Emden in Sheilos

103
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:55,560
Yaavetz Chelek Aleph Siman Kuf-samech-ches where he says

104
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:58,460
that this halacha does not really depend on

105
00:03:58,460 --> 00:04:01,520
the minhag of the place, the minhag of

106
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:04,060
the people of the place, rather it depends

107
00:04:04,060 --> 00:04:08,539
on the etzem hamakom itself. In Chutz La'aretz

108
00:04:08,539 --> 00:04:10,660
there's two days of Yom Tov, in Eretz

109
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:13,259
Yisrael there's one day of Yom Tov and

110
00:04:13,259 --> 00:04:15,906
that is it. Meaning someone who's a ben

111
00:04:15,906 --> 00:04:18,339
Eretz Yisrael that goes to visit Chutz La'aretz

112
00:04:18,339 --> 00:04:20,620
according to Rav Yaakov Emden keeps two days

113
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,899
me'ikar hadin, not just because mar'is ayin this

114
00:04:22,980 --> 00:04:26,100
that, me'ikar hadin because this minhag has nothing

115
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:27,560
to do with you, it has to do

116
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:30,339
with your location and if you are located

117
00:04:30,339 --> 00:04:32,100
in Chutz La'aretz it's two days, located in

118
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:34,336
Eretz Yisrael it's one day. The Avnei Nezer

119
00:04:34,336 --> 00:04:37,620
Orach Chaim Siman Taf-kuf-lamed-tes says something very similar

120
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:41,040
as well. Now it happens to be that

121
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:44,800
there are Rishonim that say explicitly that someone

122
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,539
who is from Chutz La'aretz and visits Eretz

123
00:04:46,539 --> 00:04:49,699
Yisrael keeps two days. Rabbeinu Chananel and the

124
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:52,420
Ravan in Pesachim Daf Nun-beis Amud Aleph where

125
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:55,233
the Gemara says amar lei Rav Safra l'Rav

126
00:04:55,233 --> 00:04:58,710
Abba kigone anan d'yadinan b'keviya d'yarcha b'yishuva lo

127
00:04:58,710 --> 00:05:02,259
avidna mahlokes. machlokes b'midbar mai, that he says

128
00:05:02,379 --> 00:05:03,920
I who happen to be familiar with the

129
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:06,500
calendar, so in the yishuv, in where people

130
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:08,680
live I don't do it because I don't

131
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:10,379
want to get involved in machlokes. But what

132
00:05:10,379 --> 00:05:12,500
about bamidbar? So what exactly is he saying?

133
00:05:12,579 --> 00:05:14,980
What's he asking? Says the Rach and the

134
00:05:15,139 --> 00:05:17,430
Ravan, Rabbeinu Chananel and the Ravan, that Rav

135
00:05:17,430 --> 00:05:19,519
Safra wanted to go to Eretz Yisrael and

136
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:22,800
was pashut that in Eretz Yisrael proper in

137
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:24,720
the yishuv he's not allowed to do melacha

138
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:26,720
on Yom Tov Sheni and his only safek

139
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:28,319
was in the midbar. So that's what he

140
00:05:28,319 --> 00:05:30,740
says: b'yishuv lo avdinan, that I'm not going

141
00:05:30,740 --> 00:05:33,019
to do melacha. That's how the Rishonim understand

142
00:05:33,019 --> 00:05:34,560
that a ben chutz la'aretz in Eretz Yisrael

143
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:37,413
may not do melacha. However, in the Sefer

144
00:05:37,413 --> 00:05:41,579
Even Shlomo on the Ravan, he suggests that

145
00:05:41,579 --> 00:05:45,100
b'yishuv lo avdinan means that lo avdinan, not

146
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:46,959
that I won't do melacha, I won't make

147
00:05:46,959 --> 00:05:48,660
a Yom Tov Sheni because I'm afraid of

148
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:51,540
Bal Tosif like the Chacham Tzvi. But the

149
00:05:51,540 --> 00:05:53,040
pashut pshat in the Ravan is like we

150
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:55,340
said, that you keep two days of Yom

151
00:05:55,340 --> 00:05:58,189
Tov. The Shulchan Aruch HaRav in Siman Tav-Tzadi-Vav

152
00:05:58,189 --> 00:06:00,579
Seif Yud-Aleph writes that bnei chutz la'aretz shebau

153
00:06:00,579 --> 00:06:03,680
l'Eretz Yisrael af al pi she'da'ato lachazor, bnei

154
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:05,560
chutz la'aretz visiting Israel even if they plan

155
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:08,432
on going home, ein osin ela yom echad

156
00:06:08,432 --> 00:06:10,639
k'vnei Eretz Yisrael. And that's why I think

157
00:06:10,639 --> 00:06:12,860
Chabad does like that, that they observe only

158
00:06:12,860 --> 00:06:14,526
one day of Yom Tov even bnei chutz

159
00:06:14,526 --> 00:06:17,420
la'aretz who visit Eretz Yisrael because the Shulchan

160
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:20,759
Aruch HaRav paskens straight like the Chacham Tzvi.

161
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:24,079
In Kuntres Acharon he quotes the Ravan, so

162
00:06:24,079 --> 00:06:26,439
even though he saw the Rishonim that disagree,

163
00:06:26,439 --> 00:06:29,519
Rishonim that disagree with the Chacham Tzvi, he

164
00:06:29,519 --> 00:06:31,500
still paskens like the Chacham Tzvi. It wasn't

165
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,439
because he didn't see the Rishonim, he himself

166
00:06:33,439 --> 00:06:36,425
quotes the Ravan. In the Sefer Ir HaKodesh

167
00:06:36,425 --> 00:06:39,860
VeHaMikdash, Rav Yechiel Michel Tucazinsky writes that the

168
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:42,759
Rav of Yerushalayim Rav Shmuel Salant held also

169
00:06:42,759 --> 00:06:45,269
that me'ikar hadin ha'halacha is like the Chacham

170
00:06:45,269 --> 00:06:47,779
Tzvi. Then there is a third sevara to

171
00:06:47,779 --> 00:06:51,090
be meikel. Rav Dov Ber Karliner in Kuntres

172
00:06:51,090 --> 00:06:55,100
HaMinhagim on page twenty-two in She'elas David has

173
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:57,899
a different sevara to perhaps be meikel. Maybe

174
00:06:57,899 --> 00:06:59,723
the whole din of Yom Tov Sheni shel

175
00:06:59,723 --> 00:07:03,300
Galuyos is only because of a chashash shema

176
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:07,300
yachzor davar l'kilkulo, that things might go back

177
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:08,879
to the way they were and we're going

178
00:07:08,879 --> 00:07:10,279
to have to be mekadesh al pi hare'iyah

179
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:13,699
and therefore you're going to keep doing things

180
00:07:13,699 --> 00:07:15,660
the way you do them now, meaning why

181
00:07:15,660 --> 00:07:17,079
is it? We're already experts in the calendar,

182
00:07:17,079 --> 00:07:18,060
we know when the real day of Yom

183
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:19,579
Tov is. So why do we still keep

184
00:07:20,319 --> 00:07:22,500
shnei yamim tovim shel galuyos? Because what happens

185
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:23,810
if we go back to being mekadesh al

186
00:07:23,810 --> 00:07:25,420
pi hare'iyah? Then we're not going to know

187
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:26,600
when Yom Tov is and then we're going

188
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:27,600
to end up observing, we're going to end

189
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:30,680
up observing one day when really we should

190
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:32,560
be observing two days. But he says that

191
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:35,500
whole sevara doesn't apply in Eretz Yisrael because

192
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:38,079
even if yachzor davar l'kilkulo in Eretz Yisrael

193
00:07:38,079 --> 00:07:39,680
we'll still be familiar, we're still going to

194
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:42,199
know which day is really Yom Tov. So

195
00:07:42,199 --> 00:07:44,420
as it turns out, there are three different

196
00:07:44,420 --> 00:07:46,839
ways in the Achronim to understand why one

197
00:07:46,839 --> 00:07:49,560
might say that a ben chutz la'aretz should

198
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:52,486
keep one day even in Eretz Yisrael. Rav

199
00:07:52,486 --> 00:07:54,120
Yaakov Emden because it doesn't depend on the

200
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:55,560
person at all, it depends on the makom.

201
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,879
The Chacham Tzvi because of the Bal Tosif

202
00:07:57,879 --> 00:07:59,819
issue, so it's not a chumra of the

203
00:07:59,819 --> 00:08:01,720
makom that you came from. And Rav Dov

204
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:04,180
Ber Karliner that in Eretz Yisrael it was

205
00:08:04,180 --> 00:08:06,139
never observed two days of Yom Tov, so

206
00:08:06,139 --> 00:08:08,149
you don't have to worry about shema yachzor

207
00:08:08,149 --> 00:08:10,779
davar l'kilkulo. L'halacha almost all the poskim are

208
00:08:10,779 --> 00:08:13,560
machmir about that issue. I mean l'halacha we

209
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:15,250
don't pasken like any of these three sevaros,

210
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:17,959
mamash a ben chutz la'aretz in Eretz Yisrael

211
00:08:17,959 --> 00:08:20,500
generally speaking for the most part we would

212
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:24,220
assume would keep two days of Yom Tov

213
00:08:24,220 --> 00:08:25,759
and not one day of Yom Tov. But

214
00:08:25,759 --> 00:08:28,459
that is not our shailah. Our shailah is

215
00:08:28,459 --> 00:08:31,759
does owning an apartment make a difference? So

216
00:08:31,759 --> 00:08:34,519
this is a very fascinating question. How do

217
00:08:34,519 --> 00:08:37,299
you decide whether you're a ben Eretz Yisrael

218
00:08:37,299 --> 00:08:39,379
or a ben chutz la'aretz? I have two

219
00:08:39,379 --> 00:08:40,720
homes. I have a home in Eretz Yisrael

220
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:42,559
and a home in chutz la'aretz. So what

221
00:08:42,559 --> 00:08:44,539
am I? I mean do I determine it

222
00:08:44,539 --> 00:08:47,019
based on which home is larger? That doesn't

223
00:08:47,019 --> 00:08:50,139
seem fair, that seems somewhat arbitrary. How exactly

224
00:08:50,139 --> 00:08:52,440
do I determine what I am? Very difficult

225
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:55,059
to find mareh mekomos on this topic. But

226
00:08:55,059 --> 00:08:56,720
leave it to Rav Asher Weiss in the

227
00:08:57,019 --> 00:09:00,659
Teshuvos Maharit Tzalon Siman Nun-Bet he says as

228
00:09:00,659 --> 00:09:04,603
follows: ve'od ani mesupak im nasa isha achas

229
00:09:04,603 --> 00:09:08,779
b'eretz yisrael ve'isha achas b'chutz la'aretz. He doesn't

230
00:09:08,779 --> 00:09:10,059
talk about a person who has two homes,

231
00:09:10,059 --> 00:09:11,559
just he talks about a person who has

232
00:09:11,559 --> 00:09:13,539
two wives. We don't recommend this. But a

233
00:09:13,539 --> 00:09:15,720
person has two wives, one in Eretz Yisrael,

234
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:19,253
